    <briefdescription>
<para>Calculate parallel checksums. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><emphasis><ref refid="interfacempp__mod_1_1mpp__chksum" kindref="compound">mpp_chksum</ref></emphasis> is a parallel checksum routine that returns an identical answer for the same array irrespective of how it has been partitioned across processors. <emphasis>int_kind</emphasis> is the KIND parameter corresponding to long integers (see discussion on OS-dependent preprocessor directives) defined in the file <ref refid="platform_8F90_source" kindref="compound">platform.F90</ref>. <emphasis>MPP_TYPE_</emphasis> corresponds to any 4-byte and 8-byte variant of <emphasis>integer</emphasis>, <emphasis>real</emphasis>, <emphasis>complex</emphasis>, <emphasis>logical</emphasis> variables, of rank 0 to 5.</para><para>Integer checksums on FP data use the F90 <computeroutput>TRANSFER()</computeroutput> intrinsic.</para><para>This provides identical results on a single-processor job, and to perform serial checksums on a single processor of a parallel job, you only need to use the optional <computeroutput>pelist</computeroutput> argument. <preformatted>
 use mpp_mod
 integer :: pe, chksum
 real :: a(:)
 pe = <ref refid="group__mpp__mod_1gacfeba7de56f9dd6000b3fd78f9d56c50" kindref="member">mpp_pe()</ref>
 chksum = <ref refid="interfacempp__mod_1_1mpp__chksum" kindref="compound">mpp_chksum</ref>( a, (/pe/) )
 </preformatted></para><para>The additional functionality of <computeroutput><ref refid="interfacempp__mod_1_1mpp__chksum" kindref="compound">mpp_chksum</ref></computeroutput> over serial checksums is to compute the checksum across the PEs in <computeroutput>pelist</computeroutput>. The answer is guaranteed to be the same for the same distributed array irrespective of how it has been partitioned.</para><para>If <computeroutput>pelist</computeroutput> is omitted, the context is assumed to be the current pelist. This call implies synchronization across the PEs in <computeroutput>pelist</computeroutput>, or the current pelist if <computeroutput>pelist</computeroutput> is absent. <linebreak/>
 Example usage: <verbatim>       mpp_chksum( var, pelist )
</verbatim></para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>var</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Data to calculate checksum of </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>pelist</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Optional list of PE&apos;s to include in checksum calculation if not using current pelist </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Parallel checksum of var across given or implicit pelist</para></simplesect>
Generic MPP_TYPE_ implentations:  mpp_chksum_  mpp_chksum_int_  mpp_chksum_int_rmask_ </para>    </detaileddescription>
